  "title": "Sophie Scholl",
  "summary": "Sophie Scholl, born 9 May 1921 in Forchtenberg, belonged to the White Rose resistance group, which distributed leaflets denouncing the Nazi regime. A caretaker detained her at the University of Munich on 18 February 1943 while she and her brother Hans distributed leaflets. The People's Court under Roland Freisler sentenced her to death, and she was executed at Munich-Stadelheim on 22 February 1943.",
